WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.499
Some things never change.

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.551
For example, mice have always been afraid of cats.

3
00:00:06.552 --> 00:00:09.894
When cats are hunting, some mice are lucky.

4
00:00:09.895 --> 00:00:12.392
Others are not.

5
00:00:12.393 --> 00:00:16.181
The mice in Cheese Town never knew when a cat might appear.

6
00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:20.439
They couldn’t tell how many cats were near.

7
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.430
There was no safe place for a mouse.

8
00:00:23.431 --> 00:00:26.449
Cats were everywhere.

9
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:30.543
Finally, the mice realized that they had to do something.

10
00:00:30.544 --> 00:00:34.528
They decided to hold a meeting.

11
00:00:34.529 --> 00:00:39.674
"Quiet, please," said Mr. Whiskers, the mayor of the mice.

12
00:00:39.675 --> 00:00:43.663
"As you know, we have a big problem with cats.

13
00:00:43.664 --> 00:00:46.380
What can we do?" he asked.

14
00:00:46.381 --> 00:00:49.071
A mouse named Luke waved his hand.

15
00:00:49.072 --> 00:00:55.352
"Yes, Luke? Do you have any ideas?" asked Mr. Whiskers.

16
00:00:55.353 --> 00:00:59.271
"We can make cat traps!" Luke said excitedly.

17
00:00:59.272 --> 00:01:04.927
"Instead of cheese, we can use fake mice."

18
00:01:04.928 --> 00:01:11.526
"Any other ideas?" Mr. Whiskers asked. "Yes, Alice?"

19
00:01:11.527 --> 00:01:15.570
"We can poison them," suggested Alice.

20
00:01:15.571 --> 00:01:22.170
"When the cats are sleeping, we can put poison in their milk."

21
00:01:22.171 --> 00:01:24.251
Mr. Whiskers shook his head.

22
00:01:24.252 --> 00:01:26.815
"Any more ideas?"

23
00:01:26.816 --> 00:01:29.762
All the mice began to speak at once.

24
00:01:29.763 --> 00:01:32.477
Every mouse had a different idea.

25
00:01:32.478 --> 00:01:37.111
Then, a wise old mouse stood up.

26
00:01:37.112 --> 00:01:40.119
He spoke slowly and quietly.

27
00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:46.480
"If we could hear a cat coming, then we could hide."

28
00:01:46.481 --> 00:01:54.447
"But how will we hear if a cat is coming?" Mr. Whiskers asked.

29
00:01:54.448 --> 00:01:57.499
The old mouse paused and thought.

30
00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:04.119
"We can tie bells around the cats' necks while they are sleeping," he said.

31
00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:09.362
"When we hear a bell, we will know a cat is coming."

32
00:02:09.363 --> 00:02:12.094
All the mice stood up and cheered.

33
00:02:12.095 --> 00:02:14.356
It was a great idea!

34
00:02:14.357 --> 00:02:19.464
It seemed like all their troubles were solved.

35
00:02:19.465 --> 00:02:25.408
"But who will tie the bells to the cats?" asked a small mouse.

36
00:02:25.409 --> 00:02:27.920
Everyone stopped cheering.

37
00:02:27.921 --> 00:02:35.892
Finally, the old mouse spoke, "Some things are easier said than done."

